  "welcomeTitle": "Welcome to Finder",
  "welcomeSubtitle": "Lost-and-found for your city: reviewed by people, matched for you, in your language.",
  "welcomeStep1Title": "Post it",
  "welcomeStep1Body": "Lost or found, add a photo and the place. A moderator checks it before it goes live.",
  "welcomeStep2Title": "Get matched",
  "welcomeStep2Body": "We alert you when a post matches yours and show every post in your app language.",
  "welcomeStep3Title": "Return it safely",
  "welcomeStep3Body": "Chat here, ask for a detail only the owner knows, and meet in a public place.",
  "welcomeHelpHint": "Step-by-step guides, including how to make sure you are talking to the real owner, are in Profile → Help & Support.",
  "welcomeGotIt": "Got it",
  "welcomeOpenHelp": "See the guides",
  "helpTileSubtitle": "Guides, safety tips and contact",
  "helpGuideTitle": "How Finder works",
  "helpGuideStartTitle": "Getting started",
  "helpGuideStartSubtitle": "Language, profile, notifications, badges",
  "helpGuideStart1": "Pick your language from the globe icon on the sign-in screen or in Profile. Every post is shown in that language.",
  "helpGuideStart2": "Complete your profile with a real name and a photo: people are more likely to return an item to someone they can recognise.",
  "helpGuideStart3": "Allow notifications so you hear about matches and messages right away.",
  "helpGuideStart4": "Badges: Pending means a moderator is still checking the post, Live means everyone can see it, Returned means the item is back with its owner.",
  "helpGuideLostTitle": "Posting a lost item",
  "helpGuideLostSubtitle": "What to include, what to keep back",
  "helpGuideLost1": "Add a clear photo of the item, or of the same model, so people recognise it at a glance.",
  "helpGuideLost2": "Give the exact place and the time you last had it. Nearby people see your post first.",
  "helpGuideLost3": "Describe it, but keep one or two details to yourself (a scratch, the contents, an engraving). You will use them to check that a finder really has it.",
  "helpGuideLost4": "A reward is optional. Never pay anything before the item is in your hands.",
  "helpGuideLost5": "Your post shows Pending until a moderator approves it, usually within a few hours. You get a notification when it is live and whenever a found post matches.",
  "helpGuideFoundTitle": "Posting a found item",
  "helpGuideFoundSubtitle": "Protect the owner while you look for them",
  "helpGuideFound1": "Photograph the item, but hide anything personal: names, ID numbers, bank cards, addresses, phone screens.",
  "helpGuideFound2": "Do not post serial numbers, IMEI or the contents of a wallet or bag. Keep them to check claims.",
  "helpGuideFound3": "Say where and when you found it and roughly where it is now. You do not have to share your home address.",
  "helpGuideFound4": "Documents, passports, phones, bank cards and money: hand them to the police or the venue's lost-property desk as well, and say so in the post.",
  "helpGuideFound5": "Once approved, the app matches your post with people searching for it and alerts them, in their own language.",
  "helpGuideMatchTitle": "When you get a match or a message",
  "helpGuideMatchSubtitle": "What to do next",
  "helpGuideMatch1": "Open the matching post and compare the photo, place and time with yours.",
  "helpGuideMatch2": "Reply inside the app chat. Keep your phone number and address private until you have met.",
  "helpGuideMatch3": "If you found the item, ask the claimant for a detail that is not in the post before you agree to meet.",
  "helpGuideMatch4": "Not the right item? Just say so politely. Someone who pressures you, asks for money or pushes to move to another app is a red flag: block and report them.",
  "helpGuideVerifyTitle": "Making sure it is the real owner",
  "helpGuideVerifySubtitle": "Simple checks that stop false claims",
  "helpGuideVerify1": "Ask for something only the owner would know: what is inside, a scratch or sticker, the lock-screen photo, an engraving, the exact colour of a strap.",
  "helpGuideVerify2": "Ask for a photo of the item from before it was lost, or a receipt, the box, or a serial number you can compare.",
  "helpGuideVerify3": "For phones: the owner can call the number or unlock it in front of you. For keys: they can name the car or open the door.",
  "helpGuideVerify4": "For documents and bank cards, hand them over only to the person named on them, with a matching ID, or to the issuing office or police.",
  "helpGuideVerify5": "Never send a deposit, transfer money or share bank details to \"release\" an item. Finder never asks for payments.",
  "helpGuideVerify6": "Still unsure? Ask to meet at a police station, or report the conversation and let a moderator look at it.",
  "helpGuideMeetTitle": "Meeting safely",
  "helpGuideMeetSubtitle": "The hand-over",
  "helpGuideMeet1": "Meet in a busy public place in daylight: a mall, a café, a police station or a lost-property desk.",
  "helpGuideMeet2": "Bring a friend or tell someone where you are going and when you expect to be back.",
  "helpGuideMeet3": "Do not get into a car or go to a private home for a hand-over.",
  "helpGuideMeet4": "Give a reward only after you have the item, and only if you offered one. Nobody can demand it.",
  "helpGuideMeet5": "Afterwards, mark the post as Returned so the alert stops and others can celebrate with you.",
  "helpGuideReportTitle": "Reporting a problem",
  "helpGuideReportSubtitle": "Posts, people, bugs",
  "helpGuideReport1": "Report a post from its menu and pick a reason. A moderator reviews it and can remove it or warn the author.",
  "helpGuideReport2": "Block a user from their profile or the chat to stop their messages. They are not told.",
  "helpGuideReport3": "Every new post is checked by a moderator, with an AI pre-check for scams, ads and inappropriate images. Approved posts can still be reported.",
  "helpGuideReport4": "Something broken? Use \"Report an issue\" below. Urgent safety matters: contact the police first."
}
